  "body": "### Summary\n\nAs a poster, I want the app to suggest the HFR smiley that matches an emoji I typed, so that my message is not truncated by the forum.\n\n### Scope\n\nBundled resource + lookup: emoji (grapheme, with and without U+FE0F) → one or more catalogue smiley codes; detector of characters HFR truncates (non-BMP, per Q-3; BMP emoji per CAP-N3 (#171)).\n\n- Module: HFRModels · Difficulty: easy · Priority: medium · post-MVP\n- Implements: FEAT-012 (#156)\n- Absorbs: FEATURES.md FEAT-012 'new emoji→smiley table'\n- Legacy sources (read-only, `origin/master`): none (legacy strips or refuses emoji: audit D 'emoji no longer stripped'); smiley catalogue `CommonSmileys.json` (LOT-012)\n- Spec: `docs/lots/LOT-096-*.md`\n\n### Depends on\n\n- LOT-012 (#45, done)\n\n### Feature umbrella\n\n- Implements FEAT-012 (#156), proposed by Bybifok (credit in the spec, PR and CREDITS.md). Other lots of this feature: LOT-151 (#241); the last lot (LOT-151 (#241)) closes #156.\n\nFEAT issues (#145–#165) are umbrellas and are never claimed: claim this lot's issue; the PR says `Closes #<this issue>` and `Refs #<FEAT issue>`.\n\n### Model\n\nSonnet → Opus (AGENTS.md §6: the reviewer is never the author model)\n\n### Captures needed\n\n- CAP-N3 (#171): Post with a BMP emoji (e.g. U+2764) and with a variation selector (U+FE0F): kept, replaced or truncated?\n\n### Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] Every suggested code exists in the bundled smiley catalogue (test).\n- [ ] Detector agrees with the LOT-048 non-BMP refusal on the same inputs; BMP emoji behaviour follows CAP-N3 (#171) or stays 'unknown' and is not refused.\n- [ ] Swift Testing tests; `swift test` green on Linux and macOS CI; module rules of docs/ARCHITECTURE.md respected (`scripts/check-lot-deps.py` passes).\n- [ ] Spec `docs/lots/LOT-096-*.md` with legacy sources (file:line), edge cases and intentional differences; verified protocol facts in HFR-PROTOCOL §6c under this lot's own `###`.\n\n### Before you start (agents and humans)\n\nRead, in order: AGENTS.md, CLAUDE.md, docs/agents/ORCHESTRATION.md, docs/agents/REVIEW-ROUNDS.md, docs/agents/LESSONS.md, CONTRIBUTING.md, docs/ARCHITECTURE.md, App/README.md, ADR 0012, the spec of every dependency (docs/lots/), docs/HFR-PROTOCOL.md for any forum fact, docs/FIXTURES.md if captures are involved. Claim with `/claim <session-id>` on this issue before writing code; PR body `Closes #<this issue>` + `Claim: <session-id>`; never guess HFR behaviour (stop and list the captures needed).",
