   "body": "**Ready for outside contributors** (steward `ext/opus-helper1`, operator decision 2026-10-29) · milestone ⚙️ M3 (board #324)\n\n**Before you start, read** (on `dev-swift`):\n- [AGENTS.md](https://github.com/ezzz/HFRnow/blob/dev-swift/AGENTS.md): the rules and the definition of done (§9)\n- [docs/agents/EXTERNAL-AGENTS.md](https://github.com/ezzz/HFRnow/blob/dev-swift/docs/agents/EXTERNAL-AGENTS.md): claims, review and merge for outside contributors\n- [docs/agents/LESSONS.md](https://github.com/ezzz/HFRnow/blob/dev-swift/docs/agents/LESSONS.md): the self-review table\n- [docs/ARCHITECTURE.md](https://github.com/ezzz/HFRnow/blob/dev-swift/docs/ARCHITECTURE.md), [docs/HFR-PROTOCOL.md](https://github.com/ezzz/HFRnow/blob/dev-swift/docs/HFR-PROTOCOL.md), [docs/FIXTURES.md](https://github.com/ezzz/HFRnow/blob/dev-swift/docs/FIXTURES.md)\n- the LOTS.md row of this lot, and its dependencies: LOT-012 ([#45](https://github.com/ezzz/HFRnow/issues/45), done; spec [LOT-012](https://github.com/ezzz/HFRnow/blob/dev-swift/docs/lots/LOT-012-form-write-models.md), with the `CommonSmileys.json` catalogue under `HFRModels/Resources/`); also the LOT-048 spec (the non-BMP refusal this table must agree with)\n\n**Spec:** you write `docs/lots/LOT-096-<name>.md` first (AGENTS.md §5 step 2), from this issue's scope, sources and acceptance criteria. This issue body is complete (scope, no legacy source, acceptance criteria). Gaps: (1) the emoji → smiley table is new public API in HFRModels, so propose its public types and names in the spec and get the core team's answer on the issue (`BLOCKED:`) before writing code; (2) the BMP-emoji behaviour is the open capture CAP-N3 ([#171](https://github.com/ezzz/HFRnow/issues/171), `host: mac`): keep it \"unknown, not refused\" as the criteria say and list it as *pending capture*, never guess; (3) the feature spec `docs/features/FEAT-012.md` does not exist on `dev-swift`: this issue and the FEATURES.md row are the spec. Feature umbrella FEAT-012 ([#156](https://github.com/ezzz/HFRnow/issues/156), proposed by Bybifok: credit in the spec, the PR and CREDITS.md); umbrellas are never claimed: the PR says `Closes #188` and `Refs #156`.\n\n**Claim:** `/claim ext/<you>-<model>-<n>`, or `CLAIM REQUEST` if you have no write access (EXTERNAL-AGENTS.md §5). The first claim wins.\n\n**Routing:** Sonnet → Opus (LOTS.md). The adversarial review may be run by **another agent of yours**, as long as it uses a different model (AGENTS.md §6). This lot is in EXTERNAL-AGENTS.md §7's list (it adds `HFRModels` public types): its review must also come from **another contributor** (`REVIEW WANTED: opus`).\n\n**Merge:** if you have no write access, the steward merges after the APPROVE and green CI. Every lot delivered by an outside contributor is also listed for the final Fable audit (#326).\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
